.TH AARU5 1 "@DATE@" "Aaru @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aaru5 \- Aaru 5.x stable data-preservation CLI (MPF-compatible)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aaru5
.RI [ options ...]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ command-options ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Aaru
is a cross-platform data preservation suite. It dumps optical and
removable media (CD, DVD, HD-DVD, Blu-ray, UMD, GameCube/Wii optical,
floppy disks, magneto-optical) to byte-perfect images, decodes their
filesystems, validates checksums, and produces metadata in the CICM
format used by preservation projects.
.PP
.B aaru5
is the stable
.B 5.4.x
release, installed under its own name so it can sit next to the rolling
.BR aaru (1)
(v6 alpha) package. It is the Aaru series that
.B MPF
(the Media Preservation Frontend) drives for floppy and optical dumping;
the v6 alpha has an incompatible command interface and does not work in
MPF. In MPF, set the Aaru executable path to
.IR /usr/bin/aaru5 .
.SH DRIVE ACCESS
.B aaru5
ships with the
.B cap_sys_rawio
file capability set, so vendor SCSI passthrough commands (optical
dumping) work without sudo.
.PP
The invoking user still needs read/write access to the device node. On a
desktop session at the local seat this is granted automatically by a
systemd-logind
.B uaccess
ACL: for optical drives
.RB ( /dev/sr* ,
.BR /dev/sg* )
by systemd itself, for floppy nodes by the udev rule this package ships.
.PP
Headless use (SSH, cron, systemd
.BR \-\-user ,
NFS-mounted device nodes) has no seat and therefore no ACL. Optical drives
remain reachable through the
.B cdrom
group:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo usermod -aG cdrom $USER
newgrp cdrom
.EE
.RE
.PP
Floppy nodes stay
.BR root:disk ,
so dumping a floppy headlessly needs root. The
.B disk
group would grant access to every block device on the system and is not a
safe substitute.
.PP
USB floppy drives enumerate as
.B root:disk
SCSI block devices
.RB ( /dev/sd* ),
which systemd does not tag
.B uaccess
by default. This package ships
.I 70\-aaru5\-floppy.rules
to add that tag, so logind grants the local-seat user an ACL on the node and
floppies dump with no group and no root. Headless sessions have no seat and
therefore no ACL; dump as root there.
.SH "COMMAND REFERENCE"
The complete command and option reference below is the help text of the
.B aaru5
binary shipped in this package, reproduced verbatim from its
.B \-\-help
output. It is regenerated from that binary at package build time, so it
always matches the installed version and cannot go stale; run
.B aaru5 \fICOMMAND\fB \-\-help
for the same text interactively.
.PP
@AARU5_COMMAND_REFERENCE@
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/aaru5
Symlink to the real binary; the kernel follows it for
.B cap_sys_rawio
inheritance on exec.
.TP
.I /usr/lib64/aaru5/
Real NativeAOT binary
.RI ( aaru )
and its bundled native SQLite provider
.RI ( libe_sqlite3.so ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/Aaru.xml
Per-user settings written by
.BR "aaru5 configure" .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Aaru/
Per-user device/media database, statistics and device reports.
.SH NOTES
On first launch Aaru builds its local database and, until
.B aaru5 configure
has been answered once, prints an EU GDPR data-sharing notice and asks
whether to enable copy-protected-media decryption. Run
.B aaru5 configure
once interactively (or opt out) to silence it.
.PP
Aaru derives its config and data paths from the application name, not the
launcher name, so
.B aaru5
reads
.I ~/.config/Aaru.xml
and
.I ~/.local/share/Aaru/
\(em the same locations a standalone
.BR aaru (1)
(v6) install uses. The settings files differ by extension (v6 uses
.IR Aaru.json ),
but the database directory is shared; if you run both as the same user
and hit a schema mismatch, point one of them at a private
.B HOME
or
.B XDG_DATA_HOME .
.PP
Upstream provides no manpage. The prose sections of this page are written by
the packager; the COMMAND REFERENCE section is not \(em it is generated at
package build time by walking the shipped binary's own
.B \-\-help
tree, so it cannot drift from the version you have installed. That is also why
the version in the header is stamped from the binary instead of being a fixed
marker: for a generated page, content and version really do move together.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aaru (1),
.BR redumper (1),
.BR discimagecreator (1)
.PP
Upstream documentation, bug tracker and release notes:
.UR https://github.com/aaru-dps/Aaru
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
Upstream lead: Natalia Portillo
.RB ( https://github.com/claunia ).
.PP
